<title>USA: U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. soybean major sales activity in the week ended Oct 3 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:  1996/97		     1997/98</p>
<p>Taiwan	108,000			   Nil</p>
<p>Mexico	 97,800</p>
<p>Malaysia     63,500</p>
<p>China	  55,000</p>
<p>Japan	  54,100</p>
<p>Net sales of 582,400 tonnes were off from the prior week by 27 percent.</p>
<p>Exports of 239,300 tonnes were 38 percent below the previous week and 23 percent below the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary export destinations: Netherlands (73,000), Malaysia (38,500), Germany (35,900) and Belgium (35,300).</p>
</text>
